##### search
$ mj index.add path="$HOME/AE/receipts" | jq -c ".data | {added, updated, unchanged}"
{"added":2,"updated":0,"unchanged":0}

$ mj trace.asset format=missing | jq -r ".data.projects[] | .projectPath, (.matches[] | \"  \" + .name, (.uses[] | \"    \" + .paths[0] + \"  (layer \" + .layer + \")\"))"
~/AE/projects/Spring Promo/Spring Promo.aep
  logo.psd
    Main > Lower Third  (layer Logo)

$ mj trace.asset format=font target="Brandon Grotesque" | jq -r ".data.projects[] | .projectPath, (.matches[] | (.uses[] | \"  \" + .paths[0] + \"  (layer \" + .layer + \")\"))"
~/AE/projects/Spring Promo/Spring Promo.aep
  Main  (layer Title)

$ mj audit.plugins target=S_Glow | jq -r ".data.projects[].projectPath"
~/AE/projects/Spring Promo/Spring Promo.aep

$ mj audit.plugins | jq -r ".data.effects[] | \"\\(.matchName)  \\(.projects) project(s)\""
ADBE Fast Blur  1 project(s)
ADBE Glo2  1 project(s)
S_Glow  1 project(s)

##### cinema4d
$ mj scene last --summary
Logo Sting.c4d (Cinema 4D 2026.3, redshift renderer)

1920 x 1080 at 24 fps, frames 0 to 71 (72 frames, 3.00 seconds).
Output: none set
Passes: Beauty, Depth.
1 camera (active: Camera).
2 materials: 1 redshift, 1 standard.
2 textures; 1 missing (tex/chrome_normal.png).
Absolute paths: /Users/ana/Desktop/env.hdr.

Heads up:
  - Missing textures: 1.

$ mj scene last
Checked Logo Sting.c4d (redshift renderer).
Found 4 problems: 1 error, 3 warnings, 0 notes.

Error: Texture "tex/chrome_normal.png" is missing.
  Why it matters: A texture file the scene points at is not on disk, so it renders as a
  missing-texture placeholder or black.
  Fix: Relink it, or use File > Save Project with Assets to collect everything beside
  the scene.
  Example, before:  tex/wood_old.png   (not found)
  Example, after:   tex/wood.png   (relinked, next to the scene)

Warning: Texture "/Users/ana/Desktop/env.hdr" uses an absolute path.
  Why it matters: An absolute texture path such as /Users/you/... exists only on your
  Mac, so the scene breaks on another machine or after a move.
  Fix: Collect assets with Save Project with Assets so paths become relative to the
  scene.
  Example, before:  /Users/me/Desktop/wood.png
  Example, after:   tex/wood.png

Warning: The render output path is empty.
  Why it matters: There is no render output path, so a render finishes without saving
  frames.
  Fix: Set the output path and format in Render Settings > Save.
  Example, before:  (empty)
  Example, after:   /work/renders/shot_$frame.png

Warning: 1 standard material in a Redshift scene.
  Why it matters: This is a Redshift scene but it contains standard materials, which
  Redshift will not shade the way you expect.
  Fix: Convert them to Redshift materials, or switch the scene to the standard/physical
  renderer.
  Example, before:  12 standard materials in a Redshift scene
  Example, after:   Redshift materials throughout

$ mj bridge last last
Logo Sting.c4d against Summer Sale.aep: 1 layer used in After Effects.
The scene is 1920 x 1080 at 24 fps, 72 frames (3.00 seconds), redshift.

Error: Comp "Sting" runs at 30 fps; the scene is 24 fps.
  Why it matters: The After Effects comp runs at a different frame rate from the Cinema
  4D scene, so frames are dropped or duplicated and motion stutters.
  Fix: Set the comp's frame rate to the scene's, or re-render the scene at the comp's
  rate.

